{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSZp1No1ETPK54cPKrTb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule below works from the sub-property's states, its case terms and the instruction's operand fields.\n\n**Units**\n- **`csr_regfile`**: kept whenever `pc` is compared, because traps redirect the pc. For register sub-properties it is cut, since ADDI-type instructions do not use the CSRs.\n- **`near_mem_icache`**: kept when `pc` is compared, because `near_mem$imem_pc` comes from the icache. Otherwise it is cut, because the instruction word is already fixed by assumption.\n- **`near_mem_dcache`**: kept only for load and store instructions, recognised by whole tokens in the description (such as `SW` or `LW`).\n\n**GPRs**\n- **`gpr0`**: always kept. It is small, and both the ILA and the RTL need x0 to be 0.\n- **Compared register in a frame sub-property** (`rd!=k`): kept, because the proof needs the start value.\n- **Compared register in a write sub-property** (`rd==k`): set to `word`. The start value is only needed when an operand field equals k, and then it is kept.\n- **Source registers fixed by `==` case terms on operand fields**: kept.\n- **Sub-properties without a case** (such as \"mem\"): if the next pc depends on a source register (JALR, recognised by whole token), all registers are kept. Otherwise the other registers are havoced.\n- **All other registers**: havoced.\n\n**Operators**\n- **Sub-properties that write `rd==k`**: per ILA node, at most one pairing is set to `uf`. The preferred pairing is the one whose RTL node is named like a destination value (`rd`/`val` tokens). Next comes one whose operand sources read the instruction opcode, `near_mem$imem_instr[6:0]`. Last comes the pairing with the most operand-source lines. No RTL node is used twice.\n- **Address operators** (`addr`/`eaddr` tokens) are preferred instead for sub-properties that compare only non-GPR states.\n- **Frame sub-properties and \"mem\"**: operators are kept. They are combinational, so this costs no state bits and avoids spurious timing counterexamples.\n\n```python\ndef tokens_of(text):\n    out = text\n    for ch in \"/.,:;()[]{}'\\\"!?=+-*&|<>\\n\\t\":\n        out = out.replace(ch, \" \")\n    return [t for t in out.split(\" \") if t != \"\"]\n\n\ndef ident_tokens(name):\n    parts = name.replace(\"$\", \"_\").split(\"_\")\n    return [p.lower() for p in parts if p != \"\"]\n\n\ndef case_value(sub, field, op):\n    for t in sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []:\n        if t.get(\"field\") == field and t.get(\"op\") == op:\n            return t.get(\"value\")\n    return None\n\n\ndef state_reg(s):\n    if len(s) >= 2 and s[0] == \"x\" and s[1:].isdigit():\n        return int(s[1:])\n    return None\n\n\ndef score_operator(c, prefer_addr):\n    toks = set(ident_tokens(c.get(\"rtl_node\", \"\")))\n    score = 0\n    if prefer_addr:\n        if \"addr\" in toks or \"eaddr\" in toks:\n            score += 10\n    else:\n        if \"rd\" in toks:\n            score += 10\n        if \"val\" in toks:\n            score += 3\n        srcs = c.get(\"rtl_operand_sources\", []) or []\n        for s in srcs:\n            if \"imem_instr[6:0]\" in s.replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\"near_mem$\", \"\"):\n                score += 5\n                break\n    score += len(c.get(\"rtl_operand_sources\", []) or []) * 0.1\n    return score\n\n\ndef choose(sub, design):\n    choices = design.get(\"choices\", [])\n    states = sub.get(\"states\", []) or []\n    fields = design.get(\"operand_fields\", []) or []\n    desc_toks = set(t.upper() for t in tokens_of(design.get(\"description\", \"\")))\n\n    is_store = any(t in desc_toks for t in [\"SB\", \"SH\", \"SW\"])\n    is_load = any(t in desc_toks for t in [\"LB\", \"LH\", \"LW\", \"LBU\", \"LHU\"])\n    is_jalr = \"JALR\" in desc_toks\n\n    has_pc = \"pc\" in states\n    gpr_states = [state_reg(s) for s in states if state_reg(s) is not None]\n    gpr_states_nz = [r for r in gpr_states if r != 0]\n    non_gpr_states = [s for s in states if state_reg(s) is None]\n\n    rd_eq = case_value(sub, \"rd\", \"==\")\n    rd_ne = case_value(sub, \"rd\", \"!=\")\n    is_write = rd_eq is not None and len(gpr_states_nz) > 0\n    is_frame = rd_ne is not None and rd_eq is None\n\n    src_regs = set()\n    for f in fields:\n        v = case_value(sub, f, \"==\")\n        if v is not None:\n            src_regs.add(int(v))\n    no_case = len(sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []) == 0\n\n    keep_all_gprs = False\n    if no_case and has_pc and len(fields) > 0 and is_jalr:\n        keep_all_gprs = True\n\n    res = {}\n    # ---- units and gprs\n    for c in choices:\n        cid = c[\"id\"]\n        kind = c.get(\"kind\")\n        levels = c.get(\"levels\", [\"keep\"])\n        if kind == \"unit\":\n            inst_toks = ident_tokens(c.get(\"instance\", \"\").replace(\".\", \"_\"))\n            lvl = \"keep\"\n            if \"csr\" in inst_toks:\n                lvl = \"keep\" if has_pc else \"cut\"\n            elif \"dcache\" in inst_toks:\n                lvl = \"keep\" if (is_store or is_load) else \"cut\"\n            elif \"icache\" in inst_toks:\n                lvl = \"keep\" if has_pc else \"cut\"\n            if lvl not in levels:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            res[cid] = lvl\n        elif kind == \"gpr\":\n            j = int(c.get(\"register\", -1))\n            if j == 0 or keep_all_gprs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif j in src_regs:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif j in gpr_states_nz:\n                if is_write:\n                    lvl = \"word\"\n                else:\n                    lvl = \"keep\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"havoc\"\n            if lvl not in levels:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            res[cid] = lvl\n\n    # ---- operators\n    ops = [c for c in choices if c.get(\"kind\") == \"operator\"]\n    for c in ops:\n        res[c[\"id\"]] = \"keep\"\n    use_uf = is_write\n    prefer_addr = False\n    if not use_uf and not is_frame and not no_case and len(non_gpr_states) > 0 \\\n            and len(gpr_states_nz) == 0 and (is_store or is_load):\n        use_uf = True\n        prefer_addr = True\n    if use_uf:\n        by_ila = {}\n        order = []\n        for c in ops:\n            if \"uf\" not in c.get(\"levels\", []):\n                continue\n            k = c.get(\"ila_node\")\n            if k not in by_ila:\n                by_ila[k] = []\n                order.append(k)\n            by_ila[k].append(c)\n        used_rtl = set()\n        for k in order:\n            cands = sorted(by_ila[k], key=lambda c: -score_operator(c, prefer_addr))\n            for c in cands:\n                rn = c.get(\"rtl_node\")\n                if rn in used_rtl:\n                    continue\n                res[c[\"id\"]] = \"uf\"\n                used_rtl.add(rn)\n                break\n    return res\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":24607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea44abb-cf0d-4c34-84c6-d1709abf5c3b","uuid":"45ddd61a-5139-453b-b4b5-2dcec3b62c7b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T10:16:14.560Z","request_id":"req_011CgSZp17fV1TYnhfnKvDHr"}
